// Generic-struct syntax: a struct declaration with a type parameter list, and a
// literal that passes a type argument. No backend implements it -- a struct's
// field layout is learned from literals and owned by one global definition, so
// Box<num> and Box<str> would share field slots and confuse field loads and the
// collector's roots. All three backends must refuse it BY NAME
// (make test-generic-structs) instead of failing later on a brace, an
// "undefined name" or a field count. See docs/TYPES_ROADMAP.md.
struct Box<T> {
  v
}
hold b = Box<num> { 1 }
show b.v
